# Dependencies left out of a package base: it is built without the optional
# feature they bring, never waits for them and does not require them.
# base<TAB>dependency<TAB>what is left out
# The dependency is an Arch package name (the recipe's depends) or a package
# base (arch/needs), each given where they differ (hip-runtime-amd of
# hip-runtime). A package of the base itself named here is not made.
plasma-nm	qt6-webengine	the Cisco AnyConnect VPN sign-in page
kdeplasma-addons	qt6-webengine	the dictionary and web browser applets
plasma-desktop	kaccounts-integration	the OpenDesktop integration plugin
purpose	kaccounts-integration	the Nextcloud and ownCloud sharing plugins
# GPU compute (CUDA, ROCm/HIP: arch/long), built without; arch/fixes turns it off
openucx	cuda	the CUDA transports
openucx	rocm-language-runtime	the ROCm transports
openucx	rocm-hip-sdk	the ROCm transports (rocm-language-runtime's base)
openucc	cuda	the CUDA execution engine and transport
openucc	nccl	the NCCL transport
openucc	hip-runtime-amd	the ROCm execution engine
openucc	hip-runtime	the ROCm execution engine (hip-runtime-amd's base)
openucc	rocm-llvm	the ROCm execution engine (its HIP compiler)
openucc	rccl	the RCCL transport
openmpi	cuda	CUDA-aware MPI
openmpi	nvidia-utils	nothing more: it was there for CUDA's libcuda.so
openmpi	hip-runtime-amd	ROCm-aware MPI
openmpi	hip-runtime	ROCm-aware MPI (hip-runtime-amd's base)
openimagedenoise	cuda	the CUDA device (NVIDIA GPUs)
openimagedenoise	hip-runtime-amd	the HIP device (AMD GPUs)
openimagedenoise	hip-runtime	the HIP device (hip-runtime-amd's base)
